---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="How to Play — Fantasy World Cup Draft Simulator"
  description="Learn how to draft a fantasy World Cup XI from historical squads, pick a formation, and run your team through a simulated knockout tournament with penalty shootouts."
>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      Guide
    </p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
        How to play the Fantasy Football World Cup
      </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-secondary">
      Build a fantasy World Cup XI from 100+ historical squads, then watch
      them battle the all-time greats through a simulated group stage and
      knockout tournament. World Cup Draft Simulator is a football simulator
      and soccer draft game where you pick a formation — 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 or
      4-2-3-1 — draft your dream team, and let the match engine simulate the
      world cup: group stage, knockout bracket, extra time and penalty
      shootouts. It's a world cup simulation and penalty shootout simulator
      built entirely around the app, so you can predict your own tournament
      outcome online, free, in the browser. In the US many players reach it as
      a soccer draft game, an online soccer game or a free soccer simulation
      game, while elsewhere it is the fantasy soccer draft and interactive
      soccer simulator they return to. There is no download and no sign-up, so
      it is the easiest browser soccer game to learn in a single sitting. The
      guide below walks through every step, from your first formation to the
      final whistle, and the FAQ answers how the soccer simulator decides
      matches and how penalty shootouts work.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-12 space-y-10">
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">1. Pick your formation</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          Choose between 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 and 4-2-3-1. Your shape locks the
          number of defenders, midfielders and attackers you can draft — every
          pick must fit a position slot.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">2. Draft your XI</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          The draft runs 12 rounds: 11 starters plus 1 bench spot. Each round
          you're offered a random nation + year roster filtered to your
          remaining slots. Use up to 3 rerolls (same nation, different year /
          different nation) before picking. Place each player onto a pitch
          slot — best-position slots are starred. Players carry tier badges
          (elite / star / standard) and chemistry updates as your squad forms.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">3. Review your squad</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          Inspect the XI on the pitch, swap players between slots or the bench,
          then start. Roles come from your formation slots — playing out of
          position is penalized, and same-nation players get a chemistry boost.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">4. Run the tournament</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          Your squad joins 3 opponents (2 weak draws, 1 strong historical team)
          in a round-robin group. Your 3 group matches play out segment by
          segment and auto-start on entry; the rest are pre-simulated. Top 2
          advance to a knockout bracket (round of 16 → quarter-final →
          semi-final → final) against fresh opponents. Ties go to extra time,
          then penalty shootouts.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-[0.5px]">5. Results &amp; replay</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
          View the final standing, squad stats, and replay any match. Lose and
          you can play again with the same team; champions get one shot only.
          Start a fresh draft any time.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

      <div class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <p>
          The full loop of World Cup Draft Simulator is shorter than it looks,
          which is the appeal of a free browser soccer game. You start by
          choosing a football formation, and because the soccer simulator
          respects positions, that choice locks how many defenders,
          midfielders and attackers you can draft across the twelve rounds — a
          4-3-3 leans attack, a 3-5-2 owns the middle, a 4-4-2 balances, and a
          4-2-3-1 controls tempo. Next the football draft simulator offers you
          a rotating board of historical World Cup squads; you place each player
          into a best-position slot, watch chemistry update, and spend a few
          rerolls when the board is unkind. Same-nation picks earn a chemistry
          boost, so a coherent world cup dream team builder beats a pile of
          stars. When your XI is set, the match engine simulates the group stage
          live, segment by segment, while the rest of the bracket is
          pre-simulated, so the entire world cup simulation resolves in moments.
          Knockout ties that stay level after extra time go to a penalty
          shootout simulator, five kicks each and then sudden death, exactly the
          drama fans remember. You are not predicting the real 2026 results —
          you are using the world cup simulator 2026 mode to predict the
          tournament you assembled, which is why players call it a world cup
          predictor for their own cup. It is a soccer game no download, so it
          runs on any device without touching storage beyond your save, and it
          is a fantasy soccer draft where the draft matters more than the
          ratings on paper. When the final whistle blows you can replay any
          match, compare squad stats, and start a fresh draft to chase a better
          outcome. The how-to-play steps above break this into five moves, and
          the FAQ below explains the football simulation, the formations and
          the penalty shootouts in plain language. However you frame it — an
          interactive soccer simulator, a world cup fantasy game, or simply the
          easiest online soccer game to open between matches — the path is the
          same: shape, draft, simulate, repeat.
        </p>
      </div>

    <div class="mt-14 border-t border-white/10 pt-10 text-center">
      <a
        href="/game"
        class="inline-block rounded-full bg-mint px-8 py-3 font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-black uppercase transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-white"
      >
        Start drafting
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-white/10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
      <p class="text-center font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
        FAQ
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-center font-display text-4xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[0.5px] sm:text-5xl">
        Questions about the simulator
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">What is World Cup Draft Simulator?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            A free browser soccer game and fantasy soccer draft tool. You build a
            dream XI from 100+ historical World Cup squads, then the app simulates
            a full tournament — group stage, knockout bracket and penalty
            shootouts — and predicts your final result.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">How does the football simulation work?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Every match is simulated segment by segment by the in-app match engine,
            factoring in player ratings, football formations and same-nation
            chemistry. The world cup simulation runs group games live and
            pre-simulates the rest of the bracket.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">What formations can I draft?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Four shapes are supported — 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 and 4-2-3-1. Your
            formation locks the defender, midfielder and attacker slots across
            the 12 draft rounds.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">How do penalty shootouts work?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Knockout ties go to extra time and then a penalty shootout simulator
            decides the winner, five kicks each before sudden death — just like
            the real world cup penalty shootouts, but generated by the game.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">Is it free and does it need a download?</h3>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Yes. It's a free soccer simulation game and browser soccer game with no
            download and no sign-up — play online on any device.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify({
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          mainEntity: [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "What is World Cup Draft Simulator?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "A free browser soccer game and fantasy soccer draft tool. You build a dream XI from 100+ historical World Cup squads, then the app simulates a full tournament — group stage, knockout bracket and penalty shootouts — and predicts your final result.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "How does the football simulation work?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Every match is simulated segment by segment by the in-app match engine, factoring in player ratings, football formations and same-nation chemistry. The world cup simulation runs group games live and pre-simulates the rest of the bracket.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "What formations can I draft?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Four shapes are supported — 4-3-3, 4-4-2, 3-5-2 and 4-2-3-1. Your formation locks the defender, midfielder and attacker slots across the 12 draft rounds.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "How do penalty shootouts work?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Knockout ties go to extra time and then a penalty shootout simulator decides the winner, five kicks each before sudden death — generated by the game.",
              },
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              name: "Is it free and does it need a download?",
              acceptedAnswer: {
                "@type": "Answer",
                text: "Yes. It's a free soccer simulation game and browser soccer game with no download and no sign-up — play online on any device.",
              },
            },
          ],
        })}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</main></Layout>
